:"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122076","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122076","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122076.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122076.patch","merged_at":"2026-08-04T16:52:30Z"},"body":"\r\nSolves #121614 \r\n\r\nBrief summary : Error log for haptic vibration error on iPhone triggers even when haptic vibration does work, this PR resolves it.\r\n\r\nI have tested the issue with MRP on demo project using `Input.vibrate_handheld()` in `func _ready():` \r\n\r\nThe original thought of code is not mine, It is taken from #121590 \r\nHowever, I have tested it and the log appears because of non-existent conditional statement which will trigger log in every case and after adding the condition, haptic logs work as expected\r\n\r\n\r\nThe issue appears a little harmless, but can make confusion to why the logs are saying haptic error when the actual haptics does work.\r\n\r\n- *Bugsquad edit:* fixes #121614 ","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.githu